# Rank 1582 / CVE-2024-47830: Plane's web frontend whitelisted every
# https host as a Next.js remote image source, so the server-side
# image optimizer fetched attacker-chosen URLs -- including internal
# addresses -- on behalf of any viewer (server-side request forgery
# through a wildcard pattern, CWE-918; PR #5452). web/next.config.js
# configured `images: { remotePatterns: [{ protocol: "https",
# hostname: "**" }], unoptimized: true }` -- the "**" hostname admits
# every host, making the allowlist a formality. Pool commit
# b9f78ba42b is the real fix (COMMIT_OK -- "chore: next image config
# updated"): the remotePatterns block is deleted entirely (with
# unoptimized images, no server-side fetch happens). No pool
# correction.
#
# ATTENTION, wildcard allowlist configuration. The guard (an
# allowlist) exists -- its pattern matches everything, the
# same over-permissive-normalization family as rank 1522's host
# checks from the configuration side: no rule can ask "does this
# allowlist entry exclude anything at all" -- a wildcard that admits
# all values is degenerate allowlist vocabulary. A binding on
# Plane's next.config would detect this application rather than the
# weakness. Measured on the real code: scanning next.config.js
# reports zero findings at both revisions. No ENGINE-GAPS.md entry.
# No definition change shipped. Spec cve_rank1582 records the
# wildcard pattern and the removed form, both asserting reject
# VYQL-RF-001: when allowlist-degeneracy vocabulary lands, the
# wildcard form must flip to expect.

test "rank1582: every https host is an allowed image source"
  lang javascript
  file web/next.config.js
  reject VYQL-RF-001
  code
  ```
  /** @type {import('next').NextConfig} */
  const nextConfig = {
    images: {
      remotePatterns: [
        {
          protocol: "https",
          hostname: "**",
        },
      ],
      unoptimized: true,
    },
  };

  module.exports = nextConfig;
  ```

test "rank1582: the fix removes the wildcard pattern"
  lang javascript
  file web/next.config.js
  reject VYQL-RF-001
  code
  ```
  /** @type {import('next').NextConfig} */
  const nextConfig = {
    images: {
      unoptimized: true,
    },
  };

  module.exports = nextConfig;
  ```
